Article 23 (Change of use by person who brings in conditional tax-free goods) (1) Where any of the following grounds arises after the goods referred to in Article 15(1) of the Act are brought into the place of bringing-in, the person who brings in such goods shall report and pay the traffic, energy, and environment tax to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of bringing-in (in cases falling under subparagraph 3, the head of the competent customs office) pursuant to Article 15(2) of the Act; provided, where the goods have received a reduction of or exemption from customs duties under the Customs Act and the person is obligated to pay the customs duties that were reduced or exempted under Article 97(3) or Article 102(2) of that Act, the importer may report and pay the traffic, energy, and environment taxes with the head of the competent customs office. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2003; Feb. 28, 2007; Feb. 2, 2012; Feb. 15, 2013; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 28, 2025>
  1. Where the person who has brought in articles falling under Article 15(1)1 or 2 of the Act alters the uses thereof or transfer the articles to another person;
  2. Where the person who has brought in a petroleum product falling under Article 15(1)3 of the Act (excluding petroleum products used to power ships for international routes or deep-sea fishery vessels) fails to submit the following documents to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of entry within six months from the date the petroleum product is brought in; provided, the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of entry may extend the period by up to three months, when it is unavoidable:
  a. In the case of a petroleum product used to power aircraft, a report on use made by the user for the petroleum product;
  b. In the case of a petroleum product used as a raw material for medical care, medicine production, fertilizer production, agricultural chemical production or the petrochemical industry, a report on use made by the user and a written verification of use issued by the head of the competent authorities;
  3. Where the person alters the use of a petroleum product used to power ships for international routes or deep-sea fishery vessels or transfers such product after he or she has submitted a detailed statement of supply of oil (in case of a deep-sea fishery vessel that is a coaster, a report of entry filed by a person who brings the relevant articles in) under Article 17(2)2, of the petroleum products mentioned in Article 15(1)3 of the Act; provided, excluded herefrom are cases where traffic, energy, and environment taxes or individual consumption taxes under the Individual Consumption Tax Act are imposed on the remainder of petroleum products brought back to Korea by ships for international routes or deep-sea fishery vessels after completing their oversea navigation or deep-sea fishery for constituting dutiable goods under Article 14 of the Customs Act.
  (2) Where any ground described in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) of this Article occurs, a person who proves a fact falling under any subparagraph of Article 15(1) of the Act shall immediately notify the Commissioner of the National Tax Service or the Commissioner of the Korea Customs Service thereof. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2003>
  (3) Where a person intends to scrap an item falling under any subparagraph of Article 15(1) of the Act, which has been brought in after having obtained approval under Article 22, because continued use thereof for the prescribed purpose is not possible due to spoilage, damage, or other reasons similar thereto, and thereby submits an application stating the following information to the head of the competent tax office and obtains his or her approval, the relevant traffic, energy, and environment tax shall not be collected: <Amended on Feb. 28, 2007>
  1. Name, address, title, and resident registration number or business registration number of the applicant;
  2. Name, quantity, standards, unit price, and price of the item, and the relevant tax amount;
  3. Quantity of the item to be scrapped and ground for scrapping;
  4. Ground for bringing the item in and the date of entry;
  5. Other references.

